  Status: draft source correspondence for
  <verbatim|manuscript/existence/selected-course-binding.tex>; not
  independently reviewed. Imported Lean source revision:
  <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464> from
  <verbatim|source/upstream.json>.

  <section|Finding><label|finding>

  The unconditional mathematical result in the manuscript is the same-family
  binding. The returned <verbatim|Run> retains <verbatim|bought : Ahead R.b
  R.Q>; specializing that continuation to the bolt, schedule, transfers and
  doors stored in the same run yields the binding for the literal
  <verbatim|R.family>. The <verbatim|Chateau> reception supplies its
  <verbatim|RankCovariance.Binding>, and the public run assembly identifies
  the family levels with the directed alloy levels.

  A separate elementary lemma proves <verbatim|Paid V a \<rightarrow\> Paid U
  a> when the three wait requests decrease coordinatewise. It treats the
  period condition as a global inequality for every schedule index and proves
  containment of the entire plateau interval, including truncated natural
  subtraction. This is a general weakening lemma, not evidence that the
  public output has a particular paid wait.

  The service construction has an intermediate upgraded wait and a universal
  franchise receipt internally. The exported selected-run interface does not
  expose that raw receipt for the final chosen run: it is consumed while
  constructing the calibrated company. This source observation alone does not
  show that downstream use is impossible: the exported <verbatim|Chateau>
  rated, warrant and market outputs may suffice for later local estimates
  without recovering the raw frequent-stage receipt. The exact question for
  the next source pass is whether those outputs supply the quantified inputs
  used by <verbatim|earn_epoch>, the bush construction and the later local
  consumers on this same <verbatim|R.family>. Do not infer a new analytic
  obstruction from the absent raw receipt. In the internal franchise receipt,
  <verbatim|Metering.cost> is a <verbatim|Launch> on the same family, stage,
  current purse and price parameters, and its <verbatim|coup> is the
  <verbatim|Corridor>; no separate launch purchase is needed if that receipt
  is used.

  <section|Exact source mapping><label|exact-source-mapping>

