  family>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Chateau>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Almandine.lean>;
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.castle>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Snow.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|Chateau.reception>
  contains <verbatim|\<exists\> B : RankCovariance.Binding C, B.world
  \<asymp\> A.B.M \<wedge\> B.prices=M.K>. <verbatim|castle> constructs this
  binding from ShapePort, exact path equality, shell domination, and the same
  Alloy/Bolt. Its proof uses Bolt sticks for path attachment and the paid
  volume/shell comparison for the larger-patch field. <verbatim|Unlatched>
  specializes to <verbatim|C=R.family> using the Run fields
  above.>>|<row|<cell|Franchise receipt and wait
  order>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.franchise>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Snow.lean>; actual caller
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.R2I.RG05Joint.richFaresWithPrediction>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Integration/RG05Preconstruction/Fares.lean>>|<cell|The
  theorem returns an upgraded wait <verbatim|Z> and a universal implication
  for every <verbatim|C>, <verbatim|Paid Z C.path.levels>, and <verbatim|B>
  with <verbatim|B.prices=K>; for each panel index it yields frequently many
  stages with Tender, Metering, ShowHours and Vents. The Fares caller
  consumes this receipt in constructing the calibrated company. The exported
  selected-run interface does not retain a proof identifying the receipt's
  <verbatim|Z> and paid-family witness with the final alloy levels of the
  fixed <verbatim|R>. The next audit should first check whether
  <verbatim|Chateau>'s exported rated/warrant/market fields bypass the need
  for this raw link. Coordinatewise weakening of <verbatim|Paid> is proved in
  the manuscript, but does not itself establish either
  route.>>|<row|<cell|Launch is already in
