  and <verbatim|background-path-convergence.tex>
  (<verbatim|sec:background-path-convergence>)>|<cell|These chapters fix one
  family/history/schedule and provide the same-history limits/services. The
  new subsection adds the same-family specialization of <verbatim|Run.bought>
  and the generic paid-wait weakening. It does not claim that these canonical
  chapters or the returned run expose the intermediate franchise receipt for
  the already selected run.>>>>>

  <section|Paid-wait weakening used><label|paid-wait-weakening-used>

  For waits over the same bar, <verbatim|U \<leq\>w V> means pointwise
  <verbatim|r_U(j)\<leq\>r_V(j)> and <verbatim|w_U(j,s)\<leq\>w_V(j,s)> for
  all stages and scales, and <verbatim|p_U\<leq\>p_V> for the minimum-period
  request. <verbatim|Paid(U,A)> has a separate global condition
  <verbatim|p_U\<leq\>P_A(i)> for every schedule index <verbatim|i>. Its
  plateau condition says that for every eligible stage <verbatim|j> there is
  a scale index <verbatim|k> with <verbatim|r_U(j)\<leq\>s_A(k)>,
  <verbatim|w_U(j,s_A(k))\<leq\>k>, and <verbatim|J_A(i)=j> throughout the
  whole truncated interval from <verbatim|k\<minus\>w_U(j,s_A(k))> to
  <verbatim|k+w_U(j,s_A(k))>.

  Under <verbatim|U\<leq\>w V>, the global period inequalities weaken
  pointwise. At each plateau, reuse the same <verbatim|k>: if
  <verbatim|a=w_U(j,s_A(k))\<leq\>b=w_V(j,s_A(k))>, then
  <verbatim|max(0,k\<minus\>b)\<leq\>max(0,k\<minus\>a)> and
  <verbatim|k+a\<leq\>k+b>. Thus the <verbatim|V> plateau interval contains
  the full <verbatim|U> interval, and its ready-time and window upper bounds
  imply the corresponding bounds for <verbatim|U>. This proves
  <verbatim|Paid(V,A)\<rightarrow\>Paid(U,A)>; no reverse implication is
  used.

  <section|Public route versus nearby alternatives><label|public-route-versus-nearby-alternatives>

  The reviewed run is produced by <verbatim|YM.Independent.constructionRun>
  through <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.R2I.RG05Joint.selectRunWithTreasuryPeriod_preselected_quote_orders_postnumeric>.
  The same-family binding supplier is <verbatim|Run.bought> on the public
  run. The franchise receipt is constructed internally along the native
  <verbatim|RG05Preconstruction/Fares> path and consumed before the exported
  run interface. The next source comparison must test the later
  <verbatim|Chateau> rated/warrant/market outputs against actual
  local-consumer inputs. This crosswalk does not treat the separate
  <verbatim|preFoundK> grantor in <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Roll/Novena.lean>
  as a substitute.

  <section|Reads and checks><label|reads-and-checks>

  Source reads were limited to the declarations listed in the table and their
  immediate caller path: <verbatim|Lean/YM/Independent/ConstructionRun.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Integration/NativePreselectedPostnumericPeriodRun.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Integration/NativeSelection/FundedCompanySelection.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Integration/NativeSelection/FundedPredictionSupply.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Integration/RG05Preconstruction/PeriodConstruction.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Integration/RG05Preconstruction/Expenses.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Integration/RG05Preconstruction/Fares.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Cross.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Forge.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Unlatch.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Rods.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Shroud/Clan.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/PCalc/Band.lean>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/Price/Intent.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/RG/History.lean>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/RANK_COVARIANCE_ATLAS/Consumer.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Almandine.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Snow.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/North/Bonus.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/RANK/Concord.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/RANK/Ratchet.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/AFTERNOON_INTERACTING_RANK_COMPARISON/Pleas.lean>,
  <verbatim|.../Soft/Postsale.lean>, <verbatim|.../Epoch.lean>,
  <verbatim|.../Leashes.lean>, <verbatim|.../Soft/Grows.lean>, and
  <verbatim|.../Soft/Coupons.lean>. Read-only parent chapters checked are the
  eight listed in the table above.

  Commands actually used: targeted <verbatim|rg -n> searches for
  <verbatim|castle>, <verbatim|franchise>, <verbatim|ShapePort>,
  <verbatim|Metering.cost>, <verbatim|Storefront>, <verbatim|Launch>,
  <verbatim|structure Run>, and family constructors; bounded <verbatim|sed
  -n> excerpts of the declarations and call sites listed above; <verbatim|ls>
  and <verbatim|pwd> to confirm the isolated clone and parent manuscript
  paths. No Lean source was edited and no Lean build was run. No full
  manuscript build or blueprint checker was run for this draft.

